1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:03,900
The same everyday moment can ask different
things of different people.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:05,500
Finding your place.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:06,700
Reading a label.

4
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,460
Following a conversation.

5
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:09,760
Asking for help.

6
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:13,480
Threadline adapts one assistant to the
support you choose.

7
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:17,040
In Memory mode, Meera asks where she left
her glasses.

8
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:19,500
Her saved words point to the kitchen table.

9
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:23,000
The assistant explains what it knows, and
what might have changed.

10
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:26,100
In Sight mode, Ravi asks about a package.

11
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:28,820
The camera helps read the visible label,
without

12
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:31,540
guessing hidden text or giving medical
directions.

13
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,800
In Hearing mode, Alex follows large, live

14
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:37,640
captions, with speaker labels that separate
voices.

15
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:40,880
In Mobility mode, Jordan asks Morgan for
help.

16
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:43,160
Threadline prepares a message to review.

17
00:00:43,740 --> 00:00:45,420
Nothing is sent without a choice.

18
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,520
One shared dashboard connects conversations,
source evidence and the next step.

19
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:54,400
These are fictional examples of a prototype,
not safety guarantees.

20
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:55,440
Threadline.

21
00:00:55,860 --> 00:00:56,640
Different needs.

22
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:58,560
One assistant that listens.
